{title: Where You Lead (Father, Hear the Prayer We Offer)}
{artist: Love Maria Willis, Samuel Longfellow / C. Michael Pilato}
{genre: Modern Worship, Hymn}
{style: Contemporary}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{tempo: 93}
{time: 6/8}
{license: Public domain}
{c: Words: Love Maria Willis, altered by Samuel Longfellow. Music: C. Michael Pilato (2018). Released into the public domain by C. Michael Pilato · Source: https://github.com/cmpilato/worship-music/tree/main/Where_You_Lead}
{c: Chords from the writer's own lead sheet (MusicXML in the source above)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Father, hear the prayer we offer.
[Cmaj7]Not for ease our prayer shall be,
[G]But for strength that we may ever
[Cmaj7]Live our lives courageously.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Not for ever in green pastures
[Cmaj7]Do we ask our way to be,
[G]But the steep and rugged pathway
[Cmaj7]May we tread rejoicingly.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Em7]Let not these words ring hollow,
[C]This [G/B]we [D]plead.
[Em7]Lord, make us brave to [C]follow
Where you [G]lead.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Not for ever by still waters
[Cmaj7]Would we idly rest and stay,
[G]But would strike the living fountains
[Cmaj7]From the rocks along our way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge}
[Em7]Be our strength in [Gmaj7/B]hours of weakness.
[Cmaj7]In our wanderings, be our guide.
[Em7]Through endeavour and [D/F#]failure and danger,
[Cmaj7/G]Father, be there [C/G]at our side.
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Let our path be bright or dreary,
[Cmaj7]Storm or sunshine be our share;
[G]May our souls in hope unweary
[Cmaj7]Make Thy work our ceaseless prayer.
{end_of_verse}
